<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia's April CPI rises 0.56 percent-official.</title>
<headline>Indonesia's April CPI rises 0.56 percent-official.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's consumer price index rose 0.56 percent month-on-month in April, compared with a decline of 0.12 percent in March, a government official said.  </p>
<p>Indonesia posted an inflation rate of 6.47 percent for the 1996 calendar year, compared with 8.64 percent in 1995.</p>
<p>The government has forecast an inflation rate of six percent for the 1997/98 fiscal year starting on April 1.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
